WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.920
Something I hear a lot from language
learners, but particularly

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:08.314
English language learners, is
the following statement:

00:00:08.314 --> 00:00:14.410
'My accent is terrible' or, 'when I 
speak English, I have an awful accent.'

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:17.670
I've been living in France for
quite a while now, and this is

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:20.800
something I often hear people
commenting on.

00:00:28.772 --> 00:00:35.700
So here at English Online, we want
to tackle the subject head on.

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:41.490
Let me ask you a question.
Do you want to have an English,

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:47.000
or Scottish or American, Canadian
or Australian accent

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:49.300
when you speak in English?

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:51.900
If you answered yes, let me
ask you a second question.

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:53.000
Why?

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:55.970
If you hear one thing from 
this video, hear this.

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:59.540
If people can understand you 
when you speak in English,

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:04.780
your accent is not an issue. If you
become confident and fluent

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:08.310
when speaking in English, it really
doesn't matter what kind

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:11.750
of accent you have. And to illustrate
this, I want to go through

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:16.800
a couple of reasons why you really,
really should embrace your accent.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:21.390
Reason number one: your accent
is the perfect icebreaker.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:25.960
Imagine you're at a party. There's
lots of people at this party.

00:01:25.970 --> 00:01:29.407
They're milling around, they're
chatting, and everybody has

00:01:29.407 --> 00:01:33.517
the same accent, so the tones
and textures of voices present

00:01:33.517 --> 00:01:35.388
in the room are all the same.

00:01:35.388 --> 00:01:38.297
Suddenly you walk in and start speaking.

00:01:38.297 --> 00:01:42.377
Uh, hello, I am Thomas. Can someone
please tell me where the toilet is?

00:01:42.387 --> 00:01:46.447
Before you know it, you're surrounded
by a group of people because

00:01:46.447 --> 00:01:48.907
they heard your accent, and they're
interested as to where you're

00:01:48.907 --> 00:01:52.287
from. Plus, you've given them something
else to talk about other

00:01:52.287 --> 00:01:55.947
than the weather or how it is that
they arrived at the party.

00:01:55.957 --> 00:02:00.384
I know you're thinking that's a massive
exaggeration, and maybe it is a little bit,

00:02:00.384 --> 00:02:05.274
but there is truth in
the fact that having a different

00:02:05.274 --> 00:02:09.764
accent to the people around you
is an icebreaker, and it does

00:02:09.774 --> 00:02:12.104
open up interesting conversations.

00:02:12.104 --> 00:02:14.904
Reason number two to embrace your accent.

00:02:14.904 --> 00:02:17.404
It shows that you are intelligent.

00:02:17.404 --> 00:02:20.604
Do you know how many people in
English-speaking countries

00:02:20.604 --> 00:02:22.242
speak more than one language?

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:27.704
36% of adults in the UK and 
23% of adults in the US.

00:02:27.794 --> 00:02:32.601
AKA, speaking a second
language is definitely not common.

00:02:32.601 --> 00:02:37.611
It's hard work to learn a second
language, so don't downplay

00:02:37.611 --> 00:02:41.081
the effort that you've gone through.
If you try to change and

00:02:41.081 --> 00:02:45.151
modify your accent to resemble
an Anglophone accent, it's almost

00:02:45.151 --> 00:02:48.331
like you're hiding all the effort
that you've gone through to

00:02:48.331 --> 00:02:50.501
learn that second language 
in the first place.

00:02:50.501 --> 00:02:54.181
I'll be bringing you some other stats 
and reasons as to why you should

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:57.100
embrace your accent in episode
two. So, see you then!

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:12.650
We are all about learning English
for the real world. Make sure

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:15.860
you subscribe so you know
when episode two comes out and in

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:20.670
the meantime, embrace your accent, 
its tones, its textures,

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:24.080
and I will see you
next time. Bye!

